description: Require an explicit architecture sketch and contracts before treating a design as ready to implement.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Napkin sketches

- Include a Mermaid diagram for the hot path and the write path before implementation.
- Name the single owner of each piece of durable state.
- Put idempotency, pagination, and error codes on the API contract, not in a follow-up.
- Label sync versus async edges.
- Call out hot rows, cross-partition transactions, and N+1 reads on the diagram itself.
- Store money and quantities as integers or exact decimals, never binary floats.
